        "original_id": "dc5ea6cc-ced6-5fb7-ae95-0409ccef6f88",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Pomona College, Brown University, Claremont Colleges consortium, Brown Bears football team\n- People: David W. Oxtoby, Charles P. Nott\n- Places: Providence, Rhode Island, United States, English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations\n- Roles: college president, football team captain\n\nFacts:\n- Brown University was founded in 1764 as the College in the English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations.\n- Brown University is the seventh-oldest institution of higher education in the United States and one of the nine colonial colleges chartered before the American Revolution.\n- Pomona College was established in 1887 and is the founding member of the Claremont Colleges consortium.\n- Charles P. Nott was the captain of the Brown Bears football team at Brown University in 1895.\n- Brown University is a private Ivy League research university in Providence, Rhode Island, United States.\n- David W. Oxtoby is an American academic who served as the ninth president of Pomona College.",
